<title>UK: Labour rules out extending VAT to food, transport.</title>
<headline>Labour rules out extending VAT to food, transport.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Labour's economics spokesman, Gordon Brown, on Monday confirmed that his party would lower value added tax on domestic fuel to five percent from eight percent if it won Britain's forthcoming election.</p>
<p>&quot;In 1994, I reaffirmed that we would not extend VAT to food, children's clothes, books and newspapers and public transport fares. That remains the position,&quot; Brown added in a keynote economic speech.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom 44-171-542 7767</p>
